{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'nl -ba src/cljc/datomworld/demo/continuation_handoff_v2.cljc'","aggregated_output":"     1\t(ns datomworld.demo.continuation-handoff-v2\n     2\t  \"Handoff payload keys for Yin VM v2 continuation transfer.\n     3\t\n     4\t   v1 handed a continuation between a register VM and a stack VM, so it needed\n     5\t   one key list per engine shape. For the ast-walker there is one payload\n     6\t   shape and one key list, and the two endpoints differ only in which VM they\n     7\t   are. The semantic VM's handoff, below, ships in-band instead.\n     8\t\n     9\t   What the payload carries: the CESK machine (`:control`, `:env`, `:k`,\n    10\t   `:store`), the scheduler (`:ready-queue`, `:wait-set`, `:parked`,\n    11\t   `:id-counter`), the observable state (`:halted?`, `:blocked?`, `:value`),\n    12\t   and the loaded program (`:program`). What it deliberately omits:\n    13\t\n    14\t   - `:in-stream` and `:in-cursor`. The v2 VM owns no program medium —\n    15\t     `dao.stream.observer` does — and `create-vm` rejects `:in-stream`.\n    16\t   - `:make-stream`, `:primitives`, `:modules`, `:bridge`, `:call-capacity`,\n    17\t     `:telemetry`. Those are composition, not execution state. `handoff->vm`\n    18\t     takes them from the receiving side's freshly constructed VM, which is\n    19\t     what makes a payload movable: a function is not a value this demo\n    20\t     pretends to serialize.\"\n    21\t  (:require [clojure.edn :as edn]\n    22\t            [clojure.walk :as walk]\n    23\t            [yin.vm.semantic :as semantic]))\n    24\t\n    25\t\n    26\t(def handoff-keys\n    27\t  [:program :control :env :k :store :parked :id-counter :ready-queue :wait-set\n    28\t   :halted? :blocked? :value])\n    29\t\n    30\t\n    31\t(defn vm-key->model\n    32\t  \"The evaluator model a vm-key names. Both endpoints are the ast-walker; the\n    33\t   keys are kept so a v2 demo reads like the v1 one it replaced.\"\n    34\t  [_vm-key]\n    35\t  :ast-walker)\n    36\t\n    37\t\n    38\t(defn vm-state->handoff\n    39\t  \"Project a v2 VM onto the portable handoff payload.\"\n    40\t  [vm-key vm-state]\n    41\t  (when vm-state\n    42\t    (assoc (select-keys vm-state handoff-keys) :vm-model (vm-key->model vm-key))))\n    43\t\n    44\t\n    45\t(defn handoff->vm-state\n    46\t  \"Rebuild a v2 VM from a handoff payload.\n    47\t\n    48\t   The base VM supplies the composition — `:make-stream`, `:primitives`,\n    49\t   `:modules`, `:bridge`, `:call-capacity` — so the payload never has to carry\n    50\t   a function. `:primitives` is not re-associated afterwards the way the v1\n    51\t   version did: the ast-walker resolves variables through the store and the\n    52\t   module registry value, not through a mutable primitives field on the\n    53\t   payload, so overwriting the base's would discard the registry this\n    54\t   composition supplied.\"\n    55\t  [vm-key payload make-vm]\n    56\t  (let [base (make-vm vm-key)]\n    57\t    (merge base (vm-state->handoff vm-key payload))))\n    58\t\n    59\t\n    60\t;; =============================================================================\n    61\t;; Semantic VM: the continuation is the datoms that travel\n    62\t;; =============================================================================\n    63\t;;\n    64\t;; A semantic VM between instructions is a code segment plus five registers —\n    65\t;; {:segment :pc :value :stack :env :k} — all plain data (yin.vm.semantic.md\n    66\t;; §7). Nothing travels off-stream: the handoff batch is the segment's\n    67\t;; `:yin.code/*` datoms followed by one registers datom whose value is EDN\n    68\t;; text, so the receiver rebuilds the machine from bytes it read, not from a\n    69\t;; host object it shares with the sender. Definitions the program made\n    70\t;; (symbol-keyed store entries) travel with the registers; primitives,\n    71\t;; modules, and the FFI pair are the receiving composition's.\n    72\t\n    73\t(def registers-attr :yin.continuation/registers)\n    74\t\n    75\t\n    76\t(def primitive-key\n    77\t  \"A host primitive on the stack or in an environment travels as\n    78\t   `{primitive-key name}` and is resolved against the receiver's primitives.\"\n    79\t  :yin.continuation/primitive)\n    80\t\n    81\t\n    82\t(defn- encode-primitives\n    83\t  \"Replace each host function in `x` with the name it has in `primitives`.\n    84\t   Throws on a host function that is not a primitive: it has no portable\n    85\t   encoding (§7 item 2).\"\n    86\t  [primitives x]\n    87\t  (let [names (into {} (map (fn [[n f]] [f n])) primitives)]\n    88\t    (walk/postwalk (fn [v]\n    89\t                     (if (fn? v)\n    90\t                       (if-let [n (get names v)]\n    91\t                         {primitive-key n}\n    92\t                         (throw (ex-info \"Cannot ship a continuation holding a host function\"\n    93\t                                         {:value (str v)})))\n    94\t                       v))\n    95\t                   x)))\n    96\t\n    97\t\n    98\t(defn- decode-primitives\n    99\t  [primitives x]\n   100\t  (walk/postwalk (fn [v]\n   101\t                   (if (and (map? v) (= 1 (count v)) (contains? v primitive-key))\n   102\t                     (or (get primitives (get v primitive-key))\n   103\t                         (throw (ex-info \"The receiver has no such primitive\"\n   104\t                                         {:name (get v primitive-key)})))\n   105\t                     v))\n   106\t                 x))\n   107\t\n   108\t\n   109\t(defn shippable?\n   110\t  \"True when a semantic VM is between instructions with nothing outside its\n   111\t   registers: no wait set, ready queue, or parked continuation, whose\n   112\t   resources are stream handles in this VM's store.\"\n   113\t  [vm-state]\n   114\t  (boolean (and vm-state\n   115\t                (:control vm-state)\n   116\t                (not (:halted? vm-state))\n   117\t                (not (:blocked? vm-state))\n   118\t                (empty? (:wait-set vm-state))\n   119\t                (empty? (:ready-queue vm-state))\n   120\t                (empty? (:parked vm-state)))))\n   121\t\n   122\t\n   123\t(defn semantic-registers\n   124\t  \"The plain-data registers of a shippable semantic VM. A primitive the\n   125\t   program resolved (a `+` pushed before its call) travels by name; any other\n   126\t   host function throws.\"\n   127\t  [vm-state]\n   128\t  (encode-primitives\n   129\t    (:primitives vm-state)\n   130\t    {:segment (get-in vm-state [:control :segment]),\n   131\t     :pc (get-in vm-state [:control :pc]),\n   132\t     :value (:value vm-state),\n   133\t     :stack (:stack vm-state),\n   134\t     :env (:env vm-state),\n   135\t     :k (:k vm-state),\n   136\t     :id-counter (:id-counter vm-state),\n   137\t     :defs (into {} (filter (comp symbol? key)) (:store vm-state))}))\n   138\t\n   139\t\n   140\t(defn continuation-datoms\n   141\t  \"The handoff batch for a shippable semantic VM running `code-datoms`: the\n   142\t   segment, then one registers datom carrying EDN text.\"\n   143\t  [code-datoms vm-state]\n   144\t  (let [registers (semantic-registers vm-state)\n   145\t        k-eid (dec (reduce min 0 (map first code-datoms)))]\n   146\t    (conj (vec code-datoms)\n   147\t          [k-eid registers-attr (pr-str registers) 0 0])))\n   148\t\n   149\t\n   150\t(defn datoms->semantic-vm\n   151\t  \"Rebuild a semantic VM from a received handoff batch: load the shipped\n   152\t   segment through the ordinary loader into `(make-vm)`, then install the\n   153\t   registers read back from EDN.\"\n   154\t  [batch make-vm]\n   155\t  (let [code (filterv #(= \"yin.code\" (namespace (nth % 1))) batch)\n   156\t        registers-datom (some #(when (= registers-attr (nth % 1)) %) batch)\n   157\t        _ (when-not registers-datom\n   158\t            (throw (ex-info \"Handoff batch carries no registers\" {:batch-size (count batch)})))\n   159\t        base (make-vm)\n   160\t        {:keys [segment pc value stack env k id-counter defs]}\n   161\t        (decode-primitives (:primitives base)\n   162\t                           (edn/read-string (nth registers-datom 2)))\n   163\t        loaded (semantic/vm-load-program base code)]\n   164\t    (when-not (= segment (:program loaded))\n   165\t      (throw (ex-info \"Handoff registers name a segment the batch does not carry\"\n   166\t                      {:segment segment, :shipped (:program loaded)})))\n   167\t    (-> loaded\n   168\t        (update :store merge defs)\n   169\t        (assoc :control {:segment segment, :pc pc}\n   170\t               :value value\n   171\t               :stack stack\n   172\t               :env env\n   173\t               :k k\n   174\t               :id-counter id-counter\n   175\t               :halted? false\n   176\t               :blocked? false))))\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
