{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_23","type":"agent_message","text":"Completed-GMT: 2026-09-13 18:55:51 GMT\nCompleted-Local: 2026-09-14 01:55:51 Asia/Ho_Chi_Minh\n\nRead-only review complete. **Changes required; no sign-off.**\n\n| Severity | file:line | invariant/evidence | recommended correction |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| P1 | [continuation_handoff_v2.cljc:114](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/datomworld/demo/continuation_handoff_v2.cljc:114) | **Axiom 4: incomplete continuation.** Immediately after `:stream-make`, `shippable?` returns true. Serialization preserves the stream reference but drops its keyword-keyed store handle. Reproduced: the receiver’s next `:stream-cursor` fails with `\"Invalid stream reference\"`. | Reject handoffs with unresolved resource dependencies before enqueueing, or serialize descriptors and explicitly reattach resources. Add a stream-creation-to-handoff regression test. |\n| P2 | [continuation_handoff_v2.cljc:101](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/datomworld/demo/continuation_handoff_v2.cljc:101) | **Pure-data fidelity:** decoding treats any singleton primitive-marker map as executable identity. Reproduced: ordinary data `{:yin.continuation/primitive '+}` becomes a host function after transfer. | Use an unambiguous tagged encoding with escaping for ordinary data; test nested literal maps and actual primitive references. |\n| P2, existing | [continuation_stream_v2.cljs:157](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljs/datomworld/demo/continuation_stream_v2.cljs:157) | **No hidden global state:** the demo retains namespace-global mutable `app-state` and `run-raf-id`; drivers access them implicitly. This predates Phase 3 but prevents unconditional invariant approval. | Give each mounted composition explicit state and scheduling ownership, with host events deposited onto a stream. |\n\nProperties that passed:\n\n- REPL `:semantic` correctly uses `(linearize/ast-loader semantic/vm-load-program)` and supplies that loader to observer coordination.\n- The semantic demo ships code datoms plus EDN register text through `enqueue-batch`; reception reconstructs a fresh VM from the batch. Its tested recursive program needs no off-stream continuation or live closure transfer.\n- REPL and observer integration retain explicit session state and separate program observation from execution.\n- Stream tests exercise make, cursor, next, put, close, blocked-read wakeup, backpressure retries, and terminal outcomes. FFI tests cover correlation, errors, and once-only handler execution.\n\n**Validation:** 69 JVM tests, 333 assertions passed across six suites. The two targeted probes above reproduced defects despite those passing tests. Browser/CLJS execution was not verified. No files were changed."}}
